cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Code for: Dormancy strategy, dispersal, and environmental predictability regulate metacommunity diversity and stability across scales"
authors:
  - family-names: Wisnoski
    given-names: Nathan I.
    affiliation: Mississippi State University
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2929-5231"
repository-code: "https://github.com/WisnoskiLab/mc-dormancy-strategies"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Simulation and analysis code for a metacommunity model in which species with
  a seasonal active stage and a bank of dormant propagules compete in patches
  whose conditions fluctuate through time. The code runs the simulations and
  draws the figures of the paper, comparing no dormancy with bet-hedging,
  anticipatory, and responsive dormancy along a gradient of dispersal rate, in
  environments that differ in temporal predictability and spatial synchrony.
keywords:
  - dormancy
  - seed bank
  - bet hedging
  - dispersal
  - metacommunity
  - stability
  - synchrony
